# AI, memory and tools

## Provider abstraction

- Roles, not models: `atlas.primary` (reasoning/conversation), `atlas.fast`
  (titles, classification, cheap steps), `atlas.extract` (structured memory
  extraction), `atlas.embed` (embeddings). Mapping lives in
  `src/core/ai/models.ts`. Swapping a vendor is a one-file change. Atlas is
  provider-independent: no vendor or model name appears outside `src/core/ai`.
  Provider clients use the lowest-retention settings available.
- Use AI SDK 7 APIs: `streamText`/`generateText` with `instructions`,
  `stopWhen: isStepCount(n)`, `toolApproval`, `timeout`, `onEnd`, `telemetry`.
  UI uses `useChat` with `DefaultChatTransport` and renders `message.parts`.
- Register telemetry once in `instrumentation.ts` (`@ai-sdk/otel`, optional
  Langfuse). Every call sets `telemetry.functionId`.
- Never log prompts or memories at info level. Redact in error paths.

## Context assembly

`assembleAtlasContext()` is pure and returns:
profile (core block) → active ventures/projects → retrieved memories (ranked)
→ recent conversation window → current message. Keep the always-in-context
core block under ~1k tokens. Retrieved memories are capped and cite their ids
so the model can reference provenance.

## Memory

- Memory rows are ADD-only with `status` (`active | superseded | rejected`)
  and `supersedes_id`. Never hard-delete; supersede. Contradictions produce a
  new row that supersedes the old.
- Every memory records `source` (`user_explicit | extracted | tool`) and
  `provenance_message_id`. Extracted memories start as `candidate` and are
  shown in a review queue; the owner confirms or rejects. Only `active`
  memories are retrieved.
- The `memory` row is canonical. Embeddings are derived and live in
  `memory_embedding` keyed by `embedding_model` (provider, model, version,
  dimensions). Only `src/core/ai/embeddings.ts` knows the provider or
  dimension; never hardcode `1536` or a model name elsewhere (ADR 0009).
- Retrieval is hybrid: pgvector cosine (HNSW) + Postgres full-text, fused
  with recency and importance weighting. Implement ranking as a pure,
  unit-tested function.
- Extraction runs after the turn completes via the `JobRunner` port, using
  `atlas.extract` with a Zod output schema. It must be idempotent per message.

## Tools and capabilities

- Every tool is a `Capability` with `id`, `description`, `inputSchema`,
  `riskLevel` (`read | write | external`), `execute`, and `requiresApproval`.
  `write`/`external` capabilities default to `toolApproval: 'user-approval'`.
- Tools receive authenticated context via `toolsContext` and never trust
  model-supplied user or workspace ids.
- Record each execution in `tool_invocation` and emit an `atlas_event`.
- The registry is the single seam for future Operatives: an Operative is a
  capability whose `execute` delegates to a sub-agent. Do not add another
  routing mechanism.

## Voice readiness

The composer is a command surface that accepts text now and audio later. Do
not couple conversation state to text input widgets. Voice will use OpenAI
Realtime over WebRTC with server-minted ephemeral tokens
(`/api/voice/session`); the API key never reaches the browser.
